  "body": "HTMLCanvasElement.prototype.toDataURL() allows any additional arguments beyond the first one. It passes them to the underlying engine, basically leaving their use implementation-defined. This seems like a potential source of incompatibility... e.g. the node-canvas implementation will take a callback as the second argument, to make the conversion async. If a browser did that, people could start depending on it, and creating browser-specific code.\n\nDoes any implementation use these extra arguments? Can we remove them?\n",
